name: dotnet-channels

High-performance thread-safe producer/consumer queues with `System.Threading.Channels`: `Channel<T>`, bounded/unbounded, backpressure, draining, hosted services. See [skill:dotnet-background-services] and [skill:dotnet-csharp-async-patterns].

Bounded channels cap memory and are preferred for production; unbounded channels grow without limit and can exhaust memory under load. `FullMode`: `Wait` blocks `WriteAsync`; `DropOldest` drops oldest; `DropNewest`/`DropWrite` drop the written item; `DropWrite` returns `false` from `TryWrite`. .NET 7 supports `itemDropped`.

await writer.WriteAsync(item, cancellationToken);
if (!writer.TryWrite(item))

Multiple producers are safe concurrently. Call `Complete()` or `TryComplete()` when production ends; `TryComplete` is idempotent.

